.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
.DS_Store
calibration/output/chains/
# Raw downloads are reproducible from data-raw/download_data.R; the MANIFEST
# (URL + access date + SHA-256 + citation) IS tracked as the provenance record.
# NB: must exclude the directory's *contents*, not the directory itself --
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
data-raw/downloads/*
!data-raw/downloads/MANIFEST.csv
# ...and the two SMALL extracts from the bulk seasonality inputs (review item
# 5c). They are ~30 KB together and they are what lets a fresh clone run
# data-raw/build_emission_seasonality.R WITHOUT re-downloading 1.2 GB of GFED
# hdf5 and a 26 MB EDGAR xlsx. The bulk inputs stay ignored; the extraction step
# that produces these is data-raw/extract_emission_seasonality.py.
!data-raw/downloads/seasonality_fire.csv
!data-raw/downloads/seasonality_fossil.csv
src/*.o
src/*.so

# testthat scratch (the "check" reporter writes these; never repo state)
tests/testthat/_problems/
tests/testthat/testthat-problems.rds

# Word lock files -- transient, never content (2026-09-24)
~$*

# Marcus's Word files in the repo root (drafts and the review comments he sends
# in) are NOT repo content. 2026-09-24 excluded only the post draft; 2026-10-15,
# before the repository went public, he ruled the review .docx untracked as well
# (the three tracked ones were removed with `git rm --cached`, still on disk).
/*.docx

# ⛔ R's DEFAULT GRAPHICS DEVICE FILE, never repo content (2026-09-25).
# Any code that draws without opening a device first -- a test, a driver, a
# console session -- makes R open `Rplots.pdf` in the working directory. Both
# copies were TRACKED, so every test run that touched a device showed up as a
# modified binary in `git status` and in every diff, which is noise that trains
# the eye to skip exactly the place a real change would appear. Nothing reads
# them (grepped). Untracked here, not deleted from disk.
Rplots.pdf
tests/testthat/Rplots.pdf

# Local, untracked Claude Code session notes (the author's private setup; 2026-10-15).
CLAUDE.local.md
